WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:11.328
"I'll capture that outlaw Robin Hood one day!" vowed the Sheriff of Nottingham.

2
00:00:11.329 --> 00:00:17.209
The sheriff was related to the man whom Robin had killed in Sherwood Forest.

3
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.389
But there was another reason the sheriff wanted to catch Robin.

4
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.868
The king was offering a generous reward: two hundred pounds!

5
00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:34.215
But no one wanted to help the sheriff find Robin—not even when he offered a reward too.

6
00:00:34.216 --> 00:00:41.226
People were afraid of the bold outlaw, and many even laughed at the sheriff.

7
00:00:41.227 --> 00:00:44.165
He'd never be able to capture Robin!

8
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:48.335
This made the sheriff very angry.

9
00:00:48.336 --> 00:00:54.747
"Robin Hood thinks he can get away with breaking the king's laws," said the sheriff to his servants.

10
00:00:54.748 --> 00:00:57.684
"Well, the king will hear about this.

11
00:00:57.685 --> 00:01:00.124
Get everything ready for a trip to London.

12
00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:02.422
We're going to see King Henry!"

13
00:01:02.423 --> 00:01:06.097
For two days the sheriff's servants prepared for the trip.

14
00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:10.924
The sheriff's men polished their armor, eager to impress the king.

15
00:01:10.925 --> 00:01:14.658
At last everyone set off for London.

16
00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:19.049
And what a sight the sheriff and his men made!

17
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:24.139
People stopped to watch them riding on their fine horses.

18
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.646
The men wore shining armor and fancy clothing.

19
00:01:28.647 --> 00:01:36.455
After two days the sheriff and his men finally reached London, where King Henry lived with Queen Eleanor.

20
00:01:36.456 --> 00:01:40.406
The sheriff and his men were led to the king.

21
00:01:40.407 --> 00:01:45.778
They bowed in front of him. "Your Majesty," said the sheriff.

22
00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:51.289
"What can I do for you, Sheriff?" asked King Henry.

23
00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.787
"Is there something that you want?"

24
00:01:55.788 --> 00:02:02.125
"As you know, that rascal Robin Hood lives near Nottingham," the sheriff began.

25
00:02:02.126 --> 00:02:05.954
"He kills your deer and robs your loyal men.

26
00:02:05.955 --> 00:02:07.757
I've tried to arrest him.

27
00:02:07.758 --> 00:02:10.478
But I haven't been able to lay a hand on him.

28
00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:13.238
I've come to beg Your Majesty for help."

29
00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:20.628
"You want my help?" The king's eyes were wide in amazement.

30
00:02:20.629 --> 00:02:25.856
"You come here with all these armed men.

31
00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:29.593
And you can't catch one thief?"

32
00:02:29.594 --> 00:02:35.664
"Well, Your Majesty, Robin is very clever," the sheriff went on.

33
00:02:35.665 --> 00:02:38.121
"He's unlike other outlaws who—"

34
00:02:38.122 --> 00:02:42.289
"Get out of my sight!" roared the king.

35
00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.927
"Go back to Nottingham and come up with a plan!

36
00:02:46.928 --> 00:02:53.636
If you can't capture Robin Hood on your own, maybe you shouldn't be sheriff!"

37
00:02:53.637 --> 00:02:57.132
"Yes, Your Majesty. I'll think of a plan, Your Majesty!"

38
00:02:57.133 --> 00:03:03.306
The sheriff backed away from the king, making one low bow after another.

39
00:03:03.307 --> 00:03:10.506
He groaned quietly to himself. "I have no idea what to do," he thought.

40
00:03:10.507 --> 00:03:13.580
The group rode slowly back to Nottingham.

41
00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:16.450
The sheriff hung his head during the trip.

42
00:03:16.451 --> 00:03:19.185
At last the sheriff's face lit up.

43
00:03:19.186 --> 00:03:22.046
"Aha!" he cried. "I've got an idea."

44
00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:24.684
"Ride quickly!" he ordered his men.

45
00:03:24.685 --> 00:03:26.482
"We have a lot of work to do.

46
00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:31.547
I know how to lure Robin Hood out of the forest and into a trap!"

47
00:03:31.548 --> 00:03:37.961
A few days later the sheriff sent messengers to deliver news across the kingdom.

48
00:03:37.962 --> 00:03:42.485
The sheriff was holding a big archery contest in Nottingham.

49
00:03:42.486 --> 00:03:45.558
First prize was a gold arrow.

50
00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:50.825
The sheriff smiled slyly, delighted with his clever idea.

51
00:03:50.826 --> 00:03:54.757
"Robin Hood won't be able to resist an archery contest.

52
00:03:54.758 --> 00:03:58.147
I'll surely be able to arrest him now!"

53
00:03:58.148 --> 00:04:03.244
And indeed Robin Hood could not resist the contest.

54
00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:08.166
As soon as he heard the news, he gathered his band of men.

55
00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.318
"Come, my merry men.

56
00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:13.013
Let's enter this shooting contest.

57
00:04:13.014 --> 00:04:16.270
There's a fine prize of a gold arrow.

58
00:04:16.271 --> 00:04:20.401
And it would annoy the sheriff if one of us won."

59
00:04:20.402 --> 00:04:26.052
"Hooray!" shouted the men. "Let's do it!"

60
00:04:26.053 --> 00:04:30.436
"Wait, my good master!" called out David of Doncaster.

61
00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:32.857
"I've just come from the Blue Boar Inn.

62
00:04:32.858 --> 00:04:36.638
I heard something very interesting from some men there.

63
00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:41.772
They say the sheriff wants you to enter the contest so he can capture you.

64
00:04:41.773 --> 00:04:43.937
I believe it's a trap, Robin.

65
00:04:43.938 --> 00:04:48.161
You must stay here in Sherwood Forest where you'll be safe."

66
00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:54.236
"Hmm. Well, maybe we won't go." Robin was quiet for a moment.

67
00:04:54.237 --> 00:04:58.857
"Oh, but I don't want the sheriff to think I'm afraid of him."

68
00:04:58.858 --> 00:05:03.919
David was worried. "I told you—it's a trap!" he said.

69
00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.735
"The inn's owner heard it straight from one of the sheriff's men.

70
00:05:07.736 --> 00:05:10.537
I beg you not to go."

71
00:05:10.538 --> 00:05:14.040
"Thank you for the warning, David," said Robin.

72
00:05:14.041 --> 00:05:19.228
"But this news actually makes the contest seem even more interesting."

73
00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:21.696
His eyes twinkled with fun.

74
00:05:21.697 --> 00:05:26.127
"We're sure to have a good time, isn't that so, men?"

75
00:05:26.128 --> 00:05:30.974
His men cheered.

76
00:05:30.975 --> 00:05:36.055
They were all looking forward to the shooting contest!

